                  },
                  "code": "IFINCREMENTALSUMMARIZATION",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "end_1772094536234",
                  "id": "1772108769395",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1772108769396_1",
                      "name": "condition",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "{{$context.$nodes.GENERATESUMMARYLOOP.$currentItem.summarizationInputMode}} == 'INCREMENTAL'"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "CONDITION"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Incremental Conversation Summary"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1772120825495"
                  },
                  "code": "INCREMENTALCONVERSATIONSUMMARY",
                  "id": "1772108845958",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1772108845959_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are an enterprise sales assistant updating an existing opportunity email-thread summary in Oracle Sales Cloud. Produce an updated consolidated summary that is strictly grounded in the new emails provided.\n\nInputs\nOpportunity context (if provided):\n{{$context.$nodes.GENERATESUMMARYLOOP.$currentItem.primaryObject.objectData}}\n\nPrior summary (previous version):\n{{$context.$nodes.GENERATESUMMARYLOOP.$currentItem.previousSummaryContext}}\n\nNew emails added since the prior summary (chronological):\n{{$context.$nodes.GENERATESUMMARYLOOP.$currentItem.engagementPayload.conversation.conversationMessages}}\n\nInstructions\n- Treat the Prior summary as the baseline. Update it using only information explicitly present in New emails.\n- Do not rehash unchanged details unless required for clarity.\n- If New emails contradict the prior summary, note the conflict under Open Questions and Risks and prefer the latest email content.\n- If a detail is missing or ambiguous, write “Not stated”. Do not guess.\n- Keep it CRM-ready: concise, action-oriented, opportunity-relevant (needs, stakeholders, scope, commercials, timeline, risks, next steps).\n- Do not include highly sensitive personal data (personal phone numbers, home addresses, payment info). Use names only as needed for stakeholder and action tracking.\n\nOutput Instructions\n- Output must be valid Markdown.\n- Use bold text for section headings only. Do not use Markdown headers.\n- Use a blank line between sections.\n- Do not include a section if there is nothing to report for that section.\n- Avoid duplication across sections\n\nOutput Template (follow exactly; omit empty sections)\n**Summary**\n- Topic Purpose: <1 concise line>\n- Why it matters: <1 concise line>\n- Sentiment: <Positive | Neutral | Negative | No specified sentiment>\n\n**Key Discussion Points**\n- <Topic>: <short statement>\n- <Topic>: <short statement>\n\n**Decisions and Commitments**\n- [<date or time cue>] <decision or commitment>. Who agreed: <name or Not stated>. Impact: <impact or Not stated>\n\n**Open Questions and Risks**\n- <item>. Owner: <name or Not stated>. Impact: <why it matters>\n\n**Next Actions**\n- <action>. Owner: <name or Not stated>. Due: <date or Not stated>. Status: <new or ongoing>\n\n**Key Dates**\n- [<date or time>] <purpose>. Attendees: <names or Not stated>"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Initial Conversation Summary"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1772121077129"
                  },
                  "code": "INITIALCONVERSATIONSUMMARY",
                  "id": "1772109172656",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1772109172658_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are an enterprise sales assistant summarising emails related to an Oracle Sales Cloud opportunity. Create a clear, action-oriented summary for a salesperson and update-ready CRM notes.\n\nInputs\nOpportunity context (if provided):\n{{$context.$nodes.GENERATESUMMARYLOOP.$currentItem.primaryObject.objectData}}\n\nEmails in this thread (chronological; include subject, sender, date, body):\n{{$context.$nodes.GENERATESUMMARYLOOP.$currentItem.engagementPayload.conversation}}\n\nInstructions\n- Summarise only what is supported by the email content. If missing or ambiguous, write “Not stated”. Do not guess.\n- Focus on opportunity-relevant items: customer needs, stakeholders, scope, commercials, timeline, risks, next steps, and explicit decisions.\n- Keep chronology for decisions and commitments using the email date when available.\n- Do not include highly sensitive personal data (personal phone numbers, home addresses, payment info). Use names only as needed.\n- Keep it concise and CRM-ready.\n\nOutput Instructions\n- Output must be valid Markdown.\n- Use bold text for section headings only. Do not use Markdown headers.\n- Use a blank line between sections.\n- Do not include a section if there is nothing to report for that section.\n- Avoid duplication across sections\n\nOutput Template (follow exactly; omit empty sections)\n**Summary**\n- Topic Purpose: <1 concise line>\n- Why it matters: <1 concise line>\n- Sentiment: <Positive | Neutral | Negative | No specified sentiment>\n\n**Key Discussion Points**\n- <Topic>: <short statement>\n- <Topic>: <short statement>\n\n**Decisions and Commitments**\n- [<date or time cue>] <decision or commitment>. Who agreed: <name or Not stated>. Impact: <impact or Not stated>\n\n**Open Questions and Risks**\n- <item>. Owner: <name or Not stated>. Impact: <why it matters>\n\n**Next Actions**\n- <action>. Owner: <name or Not stated>. Due: <date or Not stated>. Status: <new or ongoing>\n\n**Key Dates**\n- [<date or time>] <purpose>. Attendees: <names or Not stated>"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "TransformOutputA",
                    "returnType": "object",
                    "sourceCode": "const response = {};\n\nresponse.summaryRequestItemId= $context.$nodes.GENERATESUMMARYLOOP.$currentItem.summaryRequestItemId;\nresponse.summaryText= $context.$nodes.GENERATESUMMARYLOOP.INCREMENTALCONVERSATIONSUMMARY.$output;\n\nreturn response;"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "end_1772094536234"
                  },
                  "code": "TRANSFORMOUTPUTA",
                  "id": "1772120825495",
                  "inputs": [],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
                  "type": "CODE"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "TransformOutputB",
                    "returnType": "object",
                    "sourceCode": "const response = {};\n\nresponse.summaryRequestItemId= $context.$nodes.GENERATESUMMARYLOOP.$currentItem.summaryRequestItemId;\nresponse.summaryText= $context.$nodes.GENERATESUMMARYLOOP.INITIALCONVERSATIONSUMMARY.$output;\n\nreturn response;"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "end_1772094536234"
